# Sphinx of False Conclusions (4/2 flash, flying) in one game. Bot1 flashes it in during Bot2's turn 2 upkeep (CR 702.8a)
# with Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire, so it has been under Bot1's control since before turn 3 and can attack. "Whenever
# this creature attacks, draw a card, then discard a card": Bot1 draws and chooses a Forest to discard. Bot2 answers
# with a Lightning Bolt: "When this creature dies, if it isn't a token, create a token that's a copy of it" puts a token
# Sphinx onto the battlefield (CR 707.2) while the card stays in the graveyard. A second Bolt kills the token, which is a
# token, so the intervening "if" (CR 603.4) fails and nothing else is created.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Sphinx of False Conclusions
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Island
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x3
Mountain
Mountain x10

